    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d221">

                <pb facs="0243" n="229" xml:id="pg229"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 FEAC/6–1847: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Political Adviser in
                        Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Atcheson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">restricted</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-06-18T19:00:00-04:00">June 18, 1947—7
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>223. FEC 21. <hi rendition="#italic">Property of War Criminals</hi>. FEC June 12
                    adopted policy decision of above title. Text follows:</p>
                <p>[Here follows text of FEC decision (204/11) printed in <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Activities of the Far Eastern Commission</hi>, page 101.]</p>
                <p>This policy paper was delayed for some weeks in Commission because of contention
                    of some members that proceeds of confiscated property and fines should be
                    available for reparations rather than occupation costs. Eventually four veto
                    powers agreed on availability for occupation costs and dissenting members had to
                    accept decision.<anchor n="91" xml:id="d221-f1"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Marshall</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d221-f1" n="91" xml:id="d221-f1-content">
                <p>The policy decision was embodied in a directive, serial 81, June 20, sent by the
                    Joint Chiefs of Staff to SCAP as <hi rendition="#small-caps">War</hi> 80637 on
                    June 20, and a copy was sent by the Department of State to the Far Eastern
                    Commission on July 3.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
